{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Spatial Resolution.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Spatial Resolution.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"spatial resolution spatial resolution","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Spatial Resolution.md","fileName":"Spatial Resolution.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Spatial Resolution","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[XR Display Systems]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Display Systems","Output Device","Visual Display","Haptic Display","Display Fidelity","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Spatial Resolution.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Spatial Resolution.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"spatial resolution spatial resolution","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Spatial Resolution.md","fileName":"Spatial Resolution.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Spatial Resolution","heading":"Spatial Resolution","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Spatial resolution describes how finely an [[Output Device]] can distinguish or present information across space.\n\nFor a [[Visual Display]], resolution depends on both pixel count and screen size rather than pixel count alone. Viewing distance also affects perceived resolution because individual pixels become less distinguishable at greater distances. For a [[Haptic Display]], spatial resolution is the minimum spatial separation between stimuli the device can present, which should be matched to the sensitivity of the body location being stimulated.\n\nHigher resolution can improve detail, but its value depends on the user, task, viewing or contact conditions, and other parts of [[Display Fidelity]].\n\nFor a near-eye AR display, angular resolution describes how much visual angle each resolvable element occupies. Increasing pixel count without considering field of view, optics, and eye position does not by itself determine how finely registered details can be perceived.","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Display Systems","Output Device","Visual Display","Haptic Display","Display Fidelity","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Spatial Resolution.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Spatial Resolution.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"spatial resolution spatial resolution","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Spatial Resolution.md","fileName":"Spatial Resolution.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Spatial Resolution","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]\n[[augmentedreality_pearson.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Display Systems","Output Device","Visual Display","Haptic Display","Display Fidelity","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}